==Ukrainian==

===Etymology===
An early borrowing from {{bor|uk|cu|виноградъ}}, likely during {{inh|uk|orv}} based on cognates in Russian and {{cog|be|вінаград}}.  The two halves of the word are cognate to {{l|uk|вино}} and {{l|uk|город}}, with the spelling of the second element -град, marking it as a borrowing from a Slavic but not East Slavic language.

===Pronunciation===
* {{uk-IPA|виногра́д}}
* {{audio|uk|Uk-виноград.ogg|Audio}}

===Noun===
{{uk-noun|виногра́д<genu>}}

# [[vine]]
# {{lb|uk|uncountable|collectively}} [[grapes]]

